WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:02.520
- What brought you back
down there? (laughs)

00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:04.230
- Well, I wouldn't have
missed it for the world.

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:07.153
To be with Sam and Laura again, you know?

00:00:07.153 --> 00:00:08.181
(audience applauding)

00:00:08.181 --> 00:00:09.014
- Yeah.
- Yep, yep, yep, yep, yep.

00:00:09.014 --> 00:00:12.270
- Oh my god, they've changed my life.

00:00:12.270 --> 00:00:14.580
I'd be a different person
if I'd never met them.

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:16.380
They're great artists and great people.

00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:17.880
And then Colin Trevorrow,

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:19.800
who wrote it along with Emily Carmichael,

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:23.820
devised this very good way
to bring us all together.

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:26.340
I'd been a fan of hers,
I'd been a fan of his.

00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:28.290
Campbell Scott is in it, Dichen Lachman,

00:00:28.290 --> 00:00:30.513
Omar Sy is back.

00:00:31.650 --> 00:00:33.240
And it's just a great cast.
- Yeah.

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:35.910
- And Steven Spielberg
is still the godfather

00:00:35.910 --> 00:00:38.580
watchin' over the whole thing
from the start to the finish.

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:39.690
And over the decades

00:00:39.690 --> 00:00:42.697
I'd seen people come up to me and go,

00:00:42.697 --> 00:00:45.210
"Oh, my kids have seen it 100 times."

00:00:45.210 --> 00:00:46.950
- [Kelly] Oh, mine have.
- It's meant so much to us.

00:00:46.950 --> 00:00:48.480
I just love everything about it.

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:50.670
- Yeah, I agree. I agree.
(audience applauding)

00:00:50.670 --> 00:00:51.930
It's a family favorite.

00:00:51.930 --> 00:00:54.360
And it's generational, that's
what's so cool about it.

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:55.830
So y'all are new.

00:00:55.830 --> 00:00:57.360
And I was gonna say, DeWanda,

00:00:57.360 --> 00:00:58.470
I love your character.
- Thank you.

00:00:58.470 --> 00:01:00.751
- I was like, "Oh, she gonna be badass."

00:01:00.751 --> 00:01:02.380
I was like, "Show me the character!"

00:01:02.380 --> 00:01:03.213
I was very excited about it.

00:01:03.213 --> 00:01:05.310
Did you love becoming a part of this?

00:01:05.310 --> 00:01:06.660
- Yeah, it's to your point.

00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:09.530
I mean, it's the greatest
franchise of all-time.

00:01:09.530 --> 00:01:11.700
- [Kelly] It is!
- I just feel really fortunate

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:16.020
that I was back, in this beyond epic way,

00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:17.490
bringing back the legacy characters.

00:01:17.490 --> 00:01:20.513
I feel very, very grateful.

00:01:20.513 --> 00:01:21.346
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:01:21.346 --> 00:01:22.530
And Mamoudou, this is your
first time doing this too,

00:01:22.530 --> 00:01:24.300
so what was it like to be a part of it?

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:26.820
- It was nuts, yeah.
- Is it kind of intimidating?

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:28.710
'Cause you're walking on
set and you're like, "Okay."

00:01:28.710 --> 00:01:31.560
- Yeah, my first day on
set was with Laura and Sam.

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:33.330
I grew up with them watching...

00:01:33.330 --> 00:01:35.640
This was the first big blockbuster movie

00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:38.010
I ever saw as a kid, so to see them...

00:01:38.010 --> 00:01:40.980
And I admired them as
actors forever as a kid

00:01:40.980 --> 00:01:42.120
and as an adult.

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:44.670
To see them as those characters
and work opposite them,

00:01:44.670 --> 00:01:46.087
I constantly found myself just like,

00:01:46.087 --> 00:01:48.360
"Wait, am I really here?

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:49.710
Is this a real thing?"

00:01:49.710 --> 00:01:51.780
But they really made
it just so comfortable

00:01:51.780 --> 00:01:53.460
and a really pleasant experience,

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:55.380
as did these guys.
- Yeah.

00:01:55.380 --> 00:01:56.830
- [Kelly] Oh, that's awesome.

